# PINS — the rig's pinned software state, one shell-sourceable line per fact.
# This file is the single answer to "what exactly is the rig running?" and
# the cache key for any hosted lane. Advance via pins-advance.sh, weekly on
# a quiet day, NEVER mid-investigation. Kernel binaries stay on disk as
# named artifacts (~/uml-smoke/linux-<NAME>/linux), one per pin generation.
#
# Ritual on every advance: deploy -> smoke gate -> full sweeps (serial) ->
# triage delta vs committed baselines -> fold baselines -> regenerate smoke
# lists -> commit PINS + baselines together.
PIN_DATE=2026-07-24

